course: dictionary
lesson: 6759
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The same word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. The word opener is a good example. «Use the tin opener carefully, the edges are sharp» means a tool, but «The opener was the first song of the show» means the first thing in a series.
explain: Look at the words around it. Tin, can and bottle tell you it is a tool for opening things. Show, song and season tell you it is the first part of something. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence best.
explain: Sport words can be tricky too. In cricket, «The openers walked out to bat first» means the two batters who start the innings. The clue here is bat, not tins or bottles.
fact: An opener is a tool for opening something, such as a tin opener, can opener or bottle opener.
fact: An opener is the first thing in a series, such as a season opener or the first song of a show.
fact: In cricket, an opener is one of the two batters who bat first.
fact: An eye-opener is something that surprises you and teaches you something new.
fact: In writing, an opener is the first sentence or words that grab the reader, such as «Later that day» or «Meanwhile».
exercise: «Use the tin opener carefully, the edges are sharp.» What is an opener in this sentence? | The first song of a show | A batter in cricket | *A tool for opening tins | A kind of sweet
exercise: «The season opener is on Saturday.» What does opener mean here? | The last game of the year | *The first game of the season | A referee's whistle | A tool for opening bottles
exercise: Ella says an eye-opener is a tin with a lid. What does eye-opener really mean? | A cricket bat | *Something that surprises you and teaches you something new | A sad song | A tin with a lid
test: «Meanwhile, the openers walked out to bat.» In this sentence, what do openers mean? | Tools for opening tins | Eye-openers | *Cricket batters who bat first | Sentences that start a story
test: Which of these is a time opener used in writing? | *Later that day | Season opener | Bottle opener | The can opener
exam: Lila reads «He has spotted a sardine-opener, so there must be sardines somewhere.» What does sardine-opener most likely mean? | A sea where sardines live | A fish that opens its mouth | *A tool for opening sardine tins | A bottle of sardine juice
